{"version":"1","id":"ember","handle":"ember","name":"Ember Blog","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/d6044b7fc0e345d6b5d2096cfa30763e","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-7.9103,"y":-3.4046,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":134,"newest_post_at":"2023-07-08T00:00:00.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2019-10-04T00:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.003731,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.0,"avg_read_time":3.373134,"summary_length_avg":300.870968,"title_length_avg":32.291045,"title_length_var":99.116785,"tag_entropy":1.608127,"tag_diversity":0.164179,"top_tag_share":0.58209,"avg_upvotes":0.104478,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.0,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.066667,"zero_engagement_share":0.91791,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.683325,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.03876},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-8.1176,-7.5441],"cadence_depth":[1.2059,-6.0147],"hype_variety":[-2.25,-9.7059],"title_style":[-3.9118,-2.4559]},"top_tags":[["emberjs",132],["typescript",13],["general-programming",12],["javascript",7],["webdev",7],["accessibility",7],["testing",5],["css",4]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Ember 5.0 Released","The Ember Times - Issue No. 162","Accessibility Working Group Update"],"outlier":["Countdown to The New Year - Ember Template Invocation Location"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"urdrZEFNV","title":"Ember 5.1 Released","url":"https://blog.emberjs.com/ember-released-5-1","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ember-5-1-released-urdrzefnv","summary":"Ember 5.1 is an incremental, backwards compatible release of Ember with bug fixes, performance improvements, and minor deprecations. This release kicks off the 5.2 beta cycle for all sub-projects. We encourage our community to help test these beta builds and report any bugs before they are published as a final release.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ea5fd5edc4b918efb652f18b33eb739e?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-07-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"U5iFAtQlA","title":"Ember 5.0 Released","url":"https://blog.emberjs.com/ember-5-0-released","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ember-5-0-released-u5ifatqla","summary":"The Ember team has worked hard to remove all the deprecations and make us move towards Polaris. Get up-to-date with the latest in Ember and enjoy! This is the first major release under the new release strategy and goals proposed in RFC 830, Evolving Ember's Major Version Process.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ea5fd5edc4b918efb652f18b33eb739e?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-06-22T20:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"EUGDbmdkA","title":"Announcing Glint 1.0","url":"https://blog.emberjs.com/glint-1-0-released","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/announcing-glint-1-0-eugdbmdka","summary":"Glint has been available as an unstable prerelease for some time. The project has reached a level of stability and functionality that we're comfortable recommending it even for large applications. Glint enables TypeScript to understand your templates as well, meaning you get end-to-end type safety for your entire application.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ea5fd5edc4b918efb652f18b33eb739e?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-04-27T15:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"3aZjijlyc","title":"EmberConf 2023","url":"https://blog.emberjs.com/emberconf-2023","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/emberconf-2023-3azjijlyc","summary":"EmberConf 2023 will take place on July 20-21 at the Oregon Convention Center in Portland, OR. The venue is state-of-the-art and fully accessible. Tickets are on sale now! This is the first conference back in person since the pandemic.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ea5fd5edc4b918efb652f18b33eb739e?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-04-24T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"mXVKioviy","title":"EmberData 5.X Update","url":"https://blog.emberjs.com/ember-data-5-x-update-2023-04-15","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/emberdata-5-x-update-mxvkioviy","summary":"EmberData released 4.12, its final 4.x version, and began iterating towards the first release of the 5.x series. The Polaris experience for EmberData will be focused around this new request experience, working with documents (and pagination) by default, and the new presentation class.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1679501297/ea5fd5edc4b918efb652f18b33eb739e","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-04-15T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"1v9lxbBRH","title":"Ember 4.11 Released","url":"https://blog.emberjs.com/ember-released-4-11","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ember-4-11-released-1v9lxbbrh","summary":"Ember 4.11 has been released with bug fixes, performance improvements, and minor deprecations in Ember.js, Ember Data, and Ember CLI. It introduces stable TypeScript types for the '@ember/owner' and '@ember/error' packages. Ember Data 4.11.1, 4.11.2, and 4.11.3 include important bug fixes. Upgrading Ember CLI can be done using the 'ember-cli-update' project.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ea5fd5edc4b918efb652f18b33eb739e?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-05T20:37:22.164Z"},{"id":"i_SfLJPfv","title":"The Ember Times - Issue No. 205","url":"https://blog.emberjs.com/the-ember-times-issue-205","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-ember-times---issue-no-205-i-sfljpfv","summary":"Ember 4.10 has been released for ember-template-lint, the linter for best practices with Ember handlebars templates. The release also includes 5 new features for Ember.js including the introduction of the package as specified in the API for Type-Only Imports RFC, 2 bug fixes and several deprecations.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/542610a8046ebb6140b88e3e636f5dbf","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-01-30T00:37:21.751Z"},{"id":"_A1zs40kQ","title":"Ember 4.10 Released","url":"https://blog.emberjs.com/ember-released-4-10","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ember-4-10-released--a1zs40kq","summary":"Ember 4.10 is an incremental, backwards compatible release of Ember with bug fixes, performance improvements, and minor deprecations. This release kicks off the 4.11 beta cycle for all sub-projects. The ember-try addon is a great way to continuously test your projects against the latest Ember releases.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/542610a8046ebb6140b88e3e636f5dbf","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-01-29T18:13:19.820Z"},{"id":"R0rl-1YZU","title":"Ember 4.9 Released","url":"https://blog.emberjs.com/ember-4-9-released","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ember-4-9-released-r0rl-1yzu","summary":"Ember 4.9 is an incremental, backwards compatible release of Ember with bug fixes, performance improvements, and minor deprecations. This release kicks off the 4.10 beta cycle for all sub-projects. The ember-try addon is a great way to continuously test your projects against the latest Ember releases.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/542610a8046ebb6140b88e3e636f5dbf","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-12-09T03:48:04.622Z"},{"id":"tpNT_kl4E","title":"Improved RFC Process","url":"https://blog.emberjs.com/improved-rfc-process","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/improved-rfc-process-tpnt-kl4e","summary":"The Ember project is pleased to announce that an improved RFC process has been implemented. As proposed in RFC #617 \" RFC Stages\", RFCs will now progress through several stages that now include tracking implementation, release, and completeness of features, as well as design.","